"],[50922,"“victory-child” = Christ (dictionary gloss)"]]},{"slug":"rune-names","title":"Rune names","level":"Intermediate","desc":"All 34 runes of the futhorc, as rune entries.","src":"From <a href=\"#runes/alphabet\">The Runes</a> guide.","words":[[68489],[68490],[68491],[68492],[68493],[68494],[68495],[68496],[68497],[68498],[68499],[68500],[68501],[68502],[68503],[68504],[68505],[68506],[68507],[68508],[68509],[68510],[68511],[68512],[68513],[68514],[68515],[68516],[68517],[68518],[68519],[68520],[68521],[68522]]},{"slug":"survivors","title":"Words that survive in modern English","level":"Beginner","desc":"Old English words with a direct modern descendant.","src":"Each word was checked against the modern word’s etymology on <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/\">Wiktionary</a> (“inherited from Old English …”).","words":[[35589,"→ house"],[41496,"→ mother"],[9542,"→ brother"],[54180,"→ son"],[14286,"→ daughter"],[62733,"→ word"],[8925,"→ book"],[9205,"→ bread"],[33975,"→ loaf"],[33985,"→ lord"],[34306,"→ lady"],[12868,"→ queen"],[17322,"→ earl"],[11373,"→ church"],[49264,"→ ship"],[52785,"→ stone"],[64124,"→ water"],[22791,"→ fire"],[41539,"→ moon"],[15204,"→ day"],[43039,"→ night"],[23672,"→ year"],[61040,"→ week"],[47516,"→ ride"],[14613,"→ drink"],[51154,"→ sing"],[33182,"→ help"],[39289,"→ love"],[17658,"→ eat"],[33261,"→ heaven"],[63293,"→ wolf"],[7017,"→ bear"],[21729,"→ fox"],[31089,"→ goose"],[35521,"→ honey"],[50074,"→ salt"],[15745,"→ ale"],[40279,"→ mead"],[11252,"→ child"],[8717,"→ bliss"],[30737,"→ glad"],[8737,"→ blithe"],[52232,"→ sorrow"],[30913,"→ gospel"],[8661,"→ bless"]]},{"slug":"false-friends","title":"False friends","level":"Intermediate","desc":"Words that look like modern English but meant something else.","src":"The modern word’s descent and its modern meaning are from <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/\">Wiktionary</a>; the Old English meaning is the dictionary’s.","words":[[61263,"→ modern wife: “a married woman”"],[11949,"→ modern knight: “a minor nobleman with an honourable military rank”"],[13966,"→ modern deer: “a ruminant mammal with hooves and often antlers”"],[63630,"→ modern weird: “having an unusually strange character or behaviour”"],[50387,"→ modern sell: “to transfer goods or provide services in exchange for money”"],[53148,"→ modern starve: “to die because of lack of food”"],[22500,"→ modern fowl: “a bird hunted or kept for food (archaic: any bird)”"],[55417,"→ modern silly: “laughable or amusing through foolishness”"],[14314,"→ modern doom: “destiny, especially terrible”"],[15005,"→ modern dwell: “to live; to reside”"],[52531,"→ modern spill: “to drop something so that it spreads out or makes a mess”"],[59881,"→ modern wan: “pale, sickly-looking”"],[12848,"→ modern quell: “to subdue, put down, or silence”"],[41443,"→ modern mood: “a mental or emotional state”"],[53421,"→ modern stool: “a seat, especially for one person and without armrests”"],[14440,"→ modern dream: “imaginary events seen in the mind while sleeping”"],[10711,"→ modern cheap: “low or reduced in price”"]]},{"slug":"place-names","title":"Place-name elements","level":"Intermediate","desc":"Old English words hidden in English place names: -ton, -ham, -ley, -bury…","src":"Elements, modern forms and examples from Wikipedia’s “<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_elements_in_place_names_in_the_British_Isles\">List of elements in place names in the British Isles</a>”.","words":[[9881,"-bury, -borough, -burgh: Aylesbury, Canterbury"],[57394,"-ton: Skipton, Brighton"],[32260,"-ham: Nottingham, Tottenham"],[61009,"-wick, -wich: Ipswich, Norwich (the table marks it Latin/OE)"],[19813,"-ford: Bradford, Watford"],[38037,"-ley, -lea, -leigh: Barnsley"],[18120,"-field: Sheffield"],[53033,"-stead: Hampstead, Berkhamsted"],[53470,"stow: Stow-on-the-Wold, Padstow"],[36689,"-ey: Romsey"],[40506,"-mere: Windermere"],[34328,"law, low: Ludlow"],[13865,"dean, den, don: Croydon, Rottingdean (the table gives the form denu)"],[628